Protective rubber housing with a measurement stand.
Log data:
Internal memory stores 792,832 thickness readings or 20,000
waveforms with thickness data;
File name length: up to 32 characters;
9 file formats: step, sequential, sequential with user point, 2D
grid, 2D grid with user point, 3D grid, 3D user, boiler, and
manual;
Identifier of up to 20 characters (thickness measurement location
or TML);
Up to 4 notes can be stored for each identifier;
Store notes for one or multiple identification numbers.
Data Analysis:
Built-in statistical report;
Quick evaluation of readings: an integrated database table with
three programmable colors configured for specific thickness
values;
Wireless connectivity to the Link Plus app for iOS, Link-Wedge
software, or the Inspection Project Manager (IPM) application
enables easy sharing of results;
Use the GageView™software for flexible data viewing via a
wired connection.
Data Transfer:
Wireless data exchange: built-in Wi-Fi® and Bluetooth®;
Wired data transfer: USB and RS-232 communication ports;
Bidirectional transfer of settings for single-element and dual-
element probes;
File copying between internal/external microSD™memory
cards; direct export of internal files to a microSD card in CSV
format compatible with Excel;
PC software;
The GageView™interface — a Windows application — collects,
creates, prints, and manages data from the gauge. The software
communicates with the gauge through USB and RS-232 ports
and can read and write data to a microSD memory card;
Create data sets and reports;
Edit saved data;
View data set files and reviews, including thickness readings,
probe setup values, and transducer configuration values;

